  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">STEMTALENT4NL: Retention and Attraction of Highly Skilled (STEM) Talent in the Netherlands</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will contribute to the Netherlands&#x2019; efforts to ensure its attractiveness as an employment destination for highly skilled STEM graduates. This is a priority in both EU and national policy and has been included in EU &#x2018;Skills and Talent&#x2019; proposals under the EU Pact on Migration and Asylum. In the Netherlands, filling the skills shortage in the STEM sector remains a priority to which this action is most relevant. It is understood that sustainable growth in the Netherlands is predicated on attracting talent within cutting edge industries in the country.This project will assess the efficiency of the admission routes currently available. Technical assistance to the Netherlands through the provision of a comprehensive review and assessment of the Dutch Orientation Year Permit mechanism and where it sits in comparison to similar permit mechanisms delivered in other EU countries will be undertaken to build on existing research and national policies to allow public and private sector actors to create a more enabling environment in an effective manner.</narrative>
  </description>
